<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49361" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tŭbus</span></b> , i, m.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a pipe</i>,
				<i>tube.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, for conducting water, <i><span class="en">Col. 1, 5,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 42, 81, § 224</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 31, 34, §
			128</span></i>.—For wine, <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 18,
				1</span></i>.—For heating baths, <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep.
				90, 25</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> For tuba, <i>a trumpet used at sacrifices</i>, acc. to <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 117</span></i>
			Müll., and Verr. Kalend. Praenest. s. 
			 23 Mart. (<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. II. p.
				386</span></i>).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per omnes viscerum tubos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 61, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
